with debris, dirt, and dynamic lighting.\n- **Lighting**: Dramatic and contrast-heavy lighting. A mix of warm (fire/torches) and cold (moonlight) tones. Smoke and light rays to create depth.\n- **Color Palette**: Earthy tones (browns, greys) with pops of green (monster's skin) and metallic silver (warrior's armor). Accents of red for blood or glowing elements.\n- **Style Prompt**: \"Cinematic, high contrast, dramatic lighting, dynamic action poses, gritty realism, shallow depth of field in close-ups, motion blur in action, anamorphic lens flare for highlights.\"\n\n---\n\n### B) **The 5x5 Row Structure Plan**\n\n#### **Row 1 (Frames 1-5): ESTABLISHING & ATMOSPHERE**\n- Wide shots to set the stage and introduce the environment. Silhouettes of the warrior and monster.\n1. Extreme wide shot of the battlefield, showing the warrior and monster facing each other, surrounded by a destroyed, smoky landscape.\n2. Low angle wide shot of the green monster roaring, with the warrior in the distance, sword drawn.\n3. Over-the-shoulder shot from behind the warrior, looking at the monster illuminated by moonlight.\n4. Wide shot of the warrior's silhouette against a fiery background.\n5. Tracking shot of the monster's shadow stretching across the ground.\n\n#### **Row 2 (Frames 6-10): SUBJECT INTRODUCTION**\n- Medium and full-body views of the characters, showing their stances, movement, and interaction with the environment.\n6. Full-body shot of the warrior walking forward, sword at the ready, dust swirling around his feet.\n7. Medium shot of the monster smashing its fist into the ground, debris flying everywhere.\n8. Low angle medium shot of the warrior raising his shield as the monster's claw swings toward him.\n9. Side profile tracking shot of both characters circling each other in combat stance.\n10. Medium close-up of the warrior's face, sweat and determination visible, with the monster's reflection in his sword.\n\n#### **Row 3 (Frames 11-15): EMOTION & INTENSITY**\n- Close-ups of faces, eyes, and expressions to convey tension and emotion.\n11. Intense close-up of the warrior's eyes narrowing, determination clear.\n12. Close-up of the monster's glowing green eyes, filled with rage.\n13. Side close-up of the warrior's face, blood dripping from his temple, his teeth clenched.\n14. Close-up of the monster's snarling mouth, saliva spraying as it growls.\n15. Over-the-shoulder close-up of the warrior's hand gripping the hilt of his sword tightly.\n\n#### **Row 4 (Frames 16-20): SENSORY DETAILS (MACRO)**\n- Extreme close-ups of textures, hands, feet, and props to emphasize sensory details.\n16. Macro shot of the warrior's armored hand gripping the sword handle, scratches visible on the metal.\n17. Macro shot of the green monster's clawed fingers digging into the dirt, cracking the ground.\n18. Close-up of the warrior's boots stepping through mud, splashing water.\n19. Macro shot of the monster's scaly skin, with green slime dripping off.\n20. Close-up of a broken sword on the ground, blood-stained, with the reflection of the fight visible on its surface.\n\n#### **Row 5 (Frames 21-25): ACTION & CLIMAX**\n- Dynamic and intense action shots, including motion blur, dramatic angles, and a sense of resolution.\n21. High-angle shot of the monster lunging at the warrior, claws extended.\n22. Low-angle shot of the warrior sliding under the monster's swinging arm.\n23. Dutch angle shot of the warrior leaping into the air with his sword raised, ready to strike.\n24. Close-up of the sword piercing the monster's skin, green blood spraying out.\n25. Final wide shot of the warrior standing victorious over the defeated monster, with the battlefield in flames.\n\n---\n\n### C) **Master 5x5 Contact Sheet Image**\n*(I am unable to generate the actual image, but you can visualize or create it using the descriptions above. Each frame should follow the style prompt and row structure for maximum visual diversity.)*\n\n---\n\n### D) **Keyframe Text List**\nHere is 